  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Trekking in Pakistan: choosing a route</h2>
  <p>Northern Pakistan holds five of the world's fourteen 8,000-metre peaks and the longest glaciers outside the polar regions, and very few trekkers. Our treks run from Skardu, from a week to a month, and every one is camped and fully supported: guide, cook, camp crew and porters.</p>
  <p><strong>The great glacier treks.</strong> The <a href="/trekking/k2-base-camp-trek/">K2 Base Camp Trek</a> walks the Baltoro Glacier to Concordia and the foot of K2 in 21 days. The <a href="/trekking/gondogoro-la-circuit-trek/">Gondogoro La</a> follows the same route and crosses a 5,585-metre pass into the Hushe valley. The <a href="/trekking/biafo-hispar-trek/">Biafo Hispar Snow Lake Trek</a> crosses 116 kilometres of ice.</p>
  <p><strong>Shorter treks.</strong> <a href="/trekking/nangma-valley-trek/">Nangma Valley</a>, <a href="/trekking/rakaposhi-base-camp-trek/">Rakaposhi base camp</a> and <a href="/trekking/fairy-meadows-base-camp-trek/">Nanga Parbat base camp via Fairy Meadows</a> take a week to ten days and suit a first trek at altitude.</p>
  <p><strong>When to go.</strong> The high treks run from late June to early September, with July and August the most settled. See our guide to the <a href="/blog/best-time-for-trekking-in-pakistan/">best time for trekking in Pakistan</a> and our pick of the <a href="/blog/best-treks-in-pakistan/">best treks in Pakistan</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Permits.</strong> The Baltoro and the Gondogoro La are in a restricted zone, where a trekking permit and a licensed guide are required. We arrange both. Our <a href="/blog/pakistan-trekking-permits-visa/">permit and visa guide</a> explains the steps.</p>
